name: sim.persistentDataWrite
description: Deprecated. See sim.writeCustomBufferData instead.
luaSynopsis: sim.persistentDataWrite(string dataTag, string/bytes dataValue, int options = 0)
pythonSynopsis: sim.persistentDataWrite(string dataTag, buffer dataValue, int options = 0)
inputs:
1. dataTag: name of the data
2. dataValue: content of the data (which may contain any value, including embedded zeros). If dataValue is an empty string, then the data is cleared (if present).
3. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 is set (1): data is also stored on file ("system/persistentData.dat"), and automatically reloaded next time CoppeliaSim start
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: setProperty, class: app, object_setProperty.method, note: "use a 'customData.'-prefix for the property name"
- name: removeProperty, class: app, object_removeProperty.method, note: "use a 'customData.'-prefix for the property name"
